WEBVTT

00:43.252 --> 00:50.217
CHAPTER 46:
EVEN IF I HAVE TO DROP OUT

01:00.811 --> 01:01.896
What time does it start?

01:03.272 --> 01:05.524
Nine o'clock. I think.

01:06.233 --> 01:07.276
Amazing.

01:07.902 --> 01:09.945
Being summoned to
the disciplinary committee.

01:10.654 --> 01:11.739
Just eat your breakfast.

01:14.408 --> 01:16.035
Sounds like your novel's a huge hit.

01:16.535 --> 01:17.453
What's the problem?

01:17.536 --> 01:18.829
Earn money from writing.

01:19.371 --> 01:22.041
Make a killing
and give me a huge allowance.

01:23.000 --> 01:24.710
You can just drop out and take the GED.

01:31.717 --> 01:33.135
We might be your parents,

01:33.219 --> 01:35.721
but we won't necessarily take your side.

01:35.805 --> 01:38.974
We're going to accept whatever punishment
the school decides to give you.

01:39.058 --> 01:39.934
Okay?

01:40.935 --> 01:42.019
Honey…

02:00.287 --> 02:01.914
What's our game plan today?

02:04.625 --> 02:06.502
Shouldn't we present a united front?

02:09.380 --> 02:11.298
I'll go with the flow.

02:11.382 --> 02:12.299
Me too.

02:14.969 --> 02:16.971
I believe if Eui-ju hopes to keep writing

02:18.055 --> 02:19.473
and pursue it as a career,

02:21.016 --> 02:23.143
she needs to learn something from this.

02:30.651 --> 02:33.320
MURIM GIRLS' HIGH SCHOOL

02:36.782 --> 02:38.826
EPISODE 15

02:57.011 --> 02:58.387
DISCIPLINARY COMMITTEE

03:11.734 --> 03:14.278
GRADE HEAD, MS. JANG
HEAD OF STUDENT AFFAIRS, MR. SONG

03:14.361 --> 03:15.446
We are gathered today…

03:15.529 --> 03:16.614
VICE PRINCIPAL, MR. SEO

03:16.697 --> 03:17.823
…to discuss the novel

03:17.907 --> 03:23.329
written by Yeo Eui-ju
featuring her teachers as characters.

03:23.412 --> 03:26.457
I'm sure you all gathered
that the characters in the novel

03:27.207 --> 03:28.834
are based on the teachers of this school.

03:28.918 --> 03:32.671
This is a severe violation
of teachers' rights and defamation.

03:33.297 --> 03:36.216
Please share your opinions
on what we should do.

03:37.051 --> 03:37.968
Ms. Kim,

03:38.552 --> 03:41.639
I was so shaken
that I couldn't bring myself to finish it.

03:42.222 --> 03:44.725
My gosh, what a total shock.

03:46.352 --> 03:48.687
I know curiosity can prompt students
to make a mistake.

03:49.605 --> 03:50.689
However,

03:50.773 --> 03:53.984
this is when their sexual identity
and values should be forming.

03:54.068 --> 03:56.445
If one goes down the wrong path like this,

03:56.528 --> 03:58.864
we, as adults, have to correct them
sooner or later.

03:59.865 --> 04:01.951
Since she is still a minor,

04:02.034 --> 04:03.869
let's prevent her from becoming a criminal

04:04.453 --> 04:05.704
by giving her a heavy penalty.

04:06.288 --> 04:07.164
Crim…

04:08.540 --> 04:09.458
Criminal?

04:10.459 --> 04:11.835
Ms. Oh, what did you think

04:11.919 --> 04:14.004
about the novel your daughter wrote?

04:15.214 --> 04:16.173
Well…

04:16.757 --> 04:17.591
Then,

04:18.592 --> 04:21.011
let me just say a few words.

04:21.762 --> 04:25.224
Firstly, my daughter has caused
everyone gathered here

04:25.307 --> 04:28.519
discomfort and concern.

04:29.228 --> 04:31.522
For that,
I'd like to offer my sincere apology.

04:32.564 --> 04:35.526
It is all my fault
due to my shortcomings as a parent.

04:36.443 --> 04:39.905
I should have paid more attention.

04:43.075 --> 04:43.909
However!

04:47.871 --> 04:48.872
How can we as parents

04:49.915 --> 04:52.459
stop something like this?

04:55.254 --> 04:56.088
My child

04:56.714 --> 04:58.674
says it's her lifeline.

05:00.092 --> 05:01.385
She's still young,

05:02.052 --> 05:04.680
so she lacks good judgment.

05:05.889 --> 05:08.684
If you would just give her the chance
to reflect on her mistakes,

05:08.767 --> 05:10.019
I'd be truly grateful.

05:11.311 --> 05:13.814
-Please.
-Please.

05:18.944 --> 05:22.406
As the victims here, what do you think?

05:23.699 --> 05:24.825
Well…

05:24.908 --> 05:25.951
First off,

05:26.827 --> 05:30.289
I will speak on behalf of all four of us.

05:32.291 --> 05:35.085
The fact that Eui-ju
was pairing us up in her stories

05:35.169 --> 05:36.628
left us shocked and stunned.

05:38.505 --> 05:41.383
We wondered, "Is this what she fantasizes
when she looks at us?"

05:41.467 --> 05:42.301
Such thoughts

05:42.968 --> 05:44.511
gave us much discomfort too.

05:47.806 --> 05:49.058
Regarding this whole affair,

05:49.141 --> 05:50.642
we've given it a lot of thought.

05:51.310 --> 05:53.937
After much consideration,
we've come to the conclusion.

06:01.779 --> 06:03.572
What do you think we should do, ma'am?

06:07.159 --> 06:10.162
We will accept whatever you decide.

06:11.663 --> 06:12.748
Oh.

06:16.043 --> 06:17.211
What about the rest of you?

06:18.337 --> 06:20.547
Even with adaptations to reality,

06:20.631 --> 06:23.300
writing real people into a novel
without their consent

06:23.383 --> 06:24.718
is a serious matter

06:25.636 --> 06:27.304
and shouldn't be taken lightly.

06:28.138 --> 06:29.765
I hope Eui-ju will learn this lesson.

06:34.269 --> 06:36.063
We all know the saying,
"Turn the other cheek."

06:39.483 --> 06:40.317
I've…

06:41.485 --> 06:42.986
decided to do just that.

06:45.072 --> 06:46.323
What kind of nonsense is that?

06:47.074 --> 06:48.784
If we let this go
with a slap on her wrist,

06:48.867 --> 06:50.994
the school's authority will collapse.

06:51.078 --> 06:52.454
She must be expelled!

06:53.163 --> 06:54.998
I recommend expulsion.

07:02.923 --> 07:04.091
I'm the one who's responsible.

07:09.805 --> 07:11.765
I knew all about Eui-ju's novel,

07:12.391 --> 07:14.143
and I told her to keep writing.

07:22.860 --> 07:24.820
Of course, at first,
I told her to delete it.

07:24.903 --> 07:26.363
I couldn't understand her.

07:26.905 --> 07:28.115
However, Eui-ju

07:28.991 --> 07:30.784
had a clear vision for her future

07:30.868 --> 07:32.369
and was working toward her dream.

07:32.995 --> 07:34.538
Her confidence was so firm,

07:36.123 --> 07:37.749
I found myself almost envious of it.

07:43.172 --> 07:44.673
So, I encouraged her to keep writing.

07:45.299 --> 07:47.426
I wanted to trust her, watch over her,

07:48.677 --> 07:49.845
and cheer her on.

07:54.558 --> 07:55.809
Eui-ju

07:57.060 --> 08:00.230
is the type of student who sees it through
once she sets her mind to something.

08:01.565 --> 08:02.900
As her homeroom teacher,

08:02.983 --> 08:04.985
I've observed her
and come to appreciate her tenacity.

08:06.528 --> 08:08.989
Since it is Eui-ju's dream
to become a writer,

08:09.072 --> 08:12.034
please let her tenacity
blossom into a true strength,

08:13.660 --> 08:16.413
and allow her energy and passion
to help her achieve her dreams

08:17.664 --> 08:19.458
by giving her another chance.

08:21.668 --> 08:22.920
Please, just think about it.

08:34.473 --> 08:35.474
Let's hear

08:36.099 --> 08:37.517
what you intend to do.

08:38.310 --> 08:39.728
Are you going to keep writing?

08:39.811 --> 08:40.854
You won't, right?

08:44.107 --> 08:44.983
I…

08:45.567 --> 08:46.401
Yes?

08:53.075 --> 08:54.034
I…

09:00.082 --> 09:02.251
I want to keep writing.

09:03.168 --> 09:04.294
What?

09:06.380 --> 09:08.090
I will take whatever punishment
I am given,

09:09.258 --> 09:10.175
and keep on writing

09:10.926 --> 09:13.470
after crafting a story of my own
and deliberating on its elements.

09:14.888 --> 09:18.767
I've been reflecting on my actions,
and I'm sincerely sorry.

09:19.434 --> 09:21.478
I've deleted We Were Friends.

09:23.605 --> 09:25.190
However, when it comes to writing…

09:28.402 --> 09:29.778
I want to keep pursuing it.

09:32.322 --> 09:33.949
Even if I have to drop out,

09:36.201 --> 09:38.078
I will keep writing novels.

09:53.135 --> 09:55.470
I will discuss this
with the other teachers.

09:55.554 --> 09:56.722
And as for punishment,

09:57.973 --> 10:01.143
I will let you know in four days.
Let's go.

10:08.942 --> 10:09.943
-Goodbye.
-Thank you.

10:16.366 --> 10:17.451
I'm truly sorry.

10:18.035 --> 10:19.745
I'm sorry.

10:19.828 --> 10:22.873
Mr. Ga, back then,

10:23.498 --> 10:25.584
I didn't realize
you were Eui-ju's homeroom teacher.

10:25.667 --> 10:26.710
Don't worry about it.

10:27.502 --> 10:29.212
I should have looked out for her.

10:30.589 --> 10:32.507
Don't worry too much. Get home safely.

10:32.591 --> 10:33.425
Okay.

10:34.676 --> 10:36.470
I'll go and talk to Ms. Kim.

10:36.553 --> 10:37.554
-Okay.
-Sure.

10:49.107 --> 10:51.985
Mom, Dad. You can go now.

10:52.569 --> 10:53.653
Go?

10:54.780 --> 10:55.781
Oh, right.

10:55.864 --> 10:57.908
Then, we'll be off.

10:57.991 --> 10:59.368
-I'll see you at home.
-Sure.

10:59.451 --> 11:00.452
All right, then.

11:00.535 --> 11:01.745
-Goodbye.
-Have a safe trip home.

11:02.704 --> 11:03.705
Pay attention in class.

11:07.292 --> 11:08.460
You can get back to class.

11:08.543 --> 11:10.796
We have to wait for Mr. Ga.

11:16.718 --> 11:18.637
I'm sorry for what I did.

11:23.225 --> 11:25.227
I never expected to end up
in one of your early projects.

11:25.977 --> 11:28.146
I'm really sorry, Mr. Yoon.

11:29.564 --> 11:33.151
Writers observe, imagine, and write,

11:33.235 --> 11:36.488
but when dealing with real people,
we have to be careful.

11:37.072 --> 11:38.073
Do you get that now?

11:39.366 --> 11:40.200
Yes, sir.

11:40.700 --> 11:42.035
So troublesome.

11:42.119 --> 11:44.704
That letter she wrote in my class
was a big fat indicator.

11:44.788 --> 11:48.250
It was so rambling.

11:48.333 --> 11:52.379
I'm going to be keeping a close eye
on your Japanese essay assignment.

11:53.255 --> 11:55.590
If it doesn't move me emotionally,

11:55.674 --> 11:57.092
I'll give you an F for sure.

11:57.717 --> 11:58.552
Yes, sir.

11:58.635 --> 12:00.262
You're in big trouble now.

12:00.846 --> 12:02.556
Sir, I'm really sorry. I put you through--

12:02.639 --> 12:03.890
No need to apologize.

12:03.974 --> 12:05.392
I don't know much about writing anyway.

12:07.102 --> 12:08.061
But from what I hear,

12:08.687 --> 12:09.729
you have a knack for it.

12:10.856 --> 12:11.857
You do, don't you?

12:11.940 --> 12:12.941
That's all that matters.

12:14.860 --> 12:16.945
Don't worry too much.
Now, go back to class.

12:18.697 --> 12:19.531
Yes, sir.

12:26.580 --> 12:27.497
Just a moment.

12:28.748 --> 12:32.085
The more I think about it,
the more libelous it seems.

12:33.211 --> 12:34.963
I can't just forget it and move on.

12:35.046 --> 12:36.548
I simply have to

12:36.631 --> 12:39.050
retain a lawyer
and see this through to the end.

12:39.134 --> 12:41.052
He's joking.

12:41.136 --> 12:42.095
You're good to go.

12:42.179 --> 12:45.098
Why did you portray me as being so petty?

12:45.682 --> 12:46.641
Seriously though,

12:47.225 --> 12:50.353
do I look like someone who'd hide
rather than stand up to injustice?

12:50.437 --> 12:52.731
-You don't stand up to injustice.
-I do!

12:52.814 --> 12:54.024
I do, don't I?

12:55.692 --> 12:58.278
Hey, kid. What if people think
that's what I'm really like?

12:58.361 --> 13:00.280
-That is what you're like.
-No, I'm not.

13:00.363 --> 13:01.865
-You did a good job.
-Great writing.

13:01.948 --> 13:04.034
Yeah, his character was the best.

13:05.202 --> 13:06.620
Don't listen to him. Just go.

13:06.703 --> 13:07.746
-Off you go.
-Good work.

13:07.829 --> 13:09.956
Hey, you need to make some changes.

13:10.040 --> 13:11.666
Come on, revise my character!

13:16.254 --> 13:17.255
-What happened?
-Eui-ju.

13:17.339 --> 13:18.507
-Hey, Eui-ju.
-Eui-ju.

13:18.590 --> 13:20.759
-What happened?
-What did they say?

13:20.842 --> 13:22.219
-What's the verdict?
-What happened?

13:22.302 --> 13:24.596
-What's the result?
-I don't know yet.

13:24.679 --> 13:26.056
They'll discuss and let me know.

13:26.139 --> 13:27.140
-Oh, no.
-Then,

13:27.224 --> 13:29.726
are they going to let you know today?

13:29.809 --> 13:30.769
What did they say?

13:30.852 --> 13:32.479
Come on, say something.

13:32.562 --> 13:34.105
What did Mr. Ga say?

13:34.189 --> 13:35.398
Didn't he say anything?

13:35.482 --> 13:36.858
-Huh?
-To tell the truth,

13:37.859 --> 13:40.737
he already knew about it.

13:40.820 --> 13:42.697
-He caught me.
-What?

13:42.781 --> 13:45.367
-He knew about it?
-How?

13:45.450 --> 13:49.287
Since he knew and let me keep writing,

13:49.371 --> 13:51.498
he said it was his fault.

13:51.581 --> 13:52.832
Mr. Ga did?

13:52.916 --> 13:54.751
-I see.
-Really?

13:54.834 --> 13:55.919
He knew about it?

13:56.002 --> 13:58.838
-So he knew all along.
-He knew.

13:58.922 --> 14:01.049
-So what's going to happen?
-If he knew…

14:01.132 --> 14:03.009
They're having a meeting now.

14:04.719 --> 14:07.639
Her work was just as popular
as the works of established writers.

14:08.515 --> 14:09.516
If it were a real book,

14:09.599 --> 14:12.435
it would have been an instant bestseller.

14:13.436 --> 14:15.564
So what if it's popular?

14:15.647 --> 14:17.399
It's still unseemly.

14:18.483 --> 14:19.859
In the early days of online novels,

14:19.943 --> 14:22.153
there was a writer
with the pen name Love Hani.

14:22.779 --> 14:25.156
Initially, her work
received brutal criticisms,

14:25.240 --> 14:27.117
but it was so popular
that it was made into a movie.

14:28.326 --> 14:31.830
Love Hani even donated
some of her royalties to her alma mater.

14:32.789 --> 14:34.708
Think how proud the school must have been.

14:34.791 --> 14:36.251
She donated her royalties?

14:39.504 --> 14:40.880
Even so, this is unacceptable.

14:41.590 --> 14:42.841
I simply can't abide it.

14:44.634 --> 14:46.845
Mr. Song,
what are you reading so intently?

14:47.512 --> 14:49.472
Ms. Kim, the thing is,

14:49.556 --> 14:50.807
this is a big deal indeed.

14:51.308 --> 14:52.142
I said so, didn't I?

14:52.225 --> 14:53.810
It seems Eui-ju's novel

14:53.893 --> 14:56.187
is quite something.

14:56.688 --> 14:59.274
People are losing it
in the comments of her notice,

14:59.357 --> 15:00.775
asking why she took her work down.

15:00.859 --> 15:02.319
Don't be silly.

15:03.486 --> 15:04.654
How many people read it?

15:04.738 --> 15:06.865
A thousand tops?

15:07.449 --> 15:10.035
Way more than a thousand.

15:10.118 --> 15:12.162
Just counting comments alone,

15:12.245 --> 15:14.247
there are 108,420 so far.

15:14.331 --> 15:17.083
What? That many people have seen it?

15:19.544 --> 15:21.504
Even so, this is unacceptable.

15:21.588 --> 15:23.590
A student using their teachers like that.

15:23.673 --> 15:25.717
Oh, wow.

15:25.800 --> 15:28.470
They've even got a petition going.

15:28.553 --> 15:30.597
"The Committee for the Return of Imuk."

15:30.680 --> 15:31.806
Mr. Song.

15:34.476 --> 15:36.353
To be honest, my biggest concern now

15:36.436 --> 15:39.481
is the damage to the school's reputation
if the word gets out.

15:39.981 --> 15:42.233
No, we can look at it another way.

15:42.317 --> 15:46.488
"Our school cultivated a student
with this degree of literary talent."

15:47.072 --> 15:48.114
Mr. Song.

15:51.951 --> 15:53.578
That is something to be grateful for.

15:55.747 --> 15:58.083
She could become a famous writer
like what's-her-name

15:58.166 --> 16:00.126
who wrote the Harry Potter series.

16:00.210 --> 16:01.920
Anything's possible, right?

16:02.462 --> 16:03.588
Sure.

16:03.672 --> 16:04.756
You're so right, ma'am.

16:05.840 --> 16:06.758
Let me think.

16:09.344 --> 16:10.679
What should we do?

16:15.767 --> 16:19.104
4 DAYS LATER

16:21.981 --> 16:24.484
Your actions in this instance

16:24.567 --> 16:27.278
were not only a serious violation
of school regulations,

16:27.362 --> 16:31.491
but also had a negative impact
on other students.

16:36.329 --> 16:38.665
However, since you have shown contrition,

16:38.748 --> 16:41.376
we acknowledge your willingness to reform.

16:41.459 --> 16:44.212
As such, we'll give you one last chance.

16:44.921 --> 16:46.423
You will be punished,

16:46.923 --> 16:49.509
but we will not stop you
from pursuing your dream.

16:51.136 --> 16:55.473
Accordingly, the school's decision
on this matter is…

17:05.817 --> 17:07.444
that you will be suspended for five days.

17:18.997 --> 17:19.873
One more thing,

17:20.999 --> 17:21.958
am I in it too?

17:24.169 --> 17:26.212
-What happened?
-What did you get?

17:26.838 --> 17:27.881
Suspended…

17:29.048 --> 17:30.091
for five days.

17:30.925 --> 17:31.885
-Suspended?
-Suspended?

17:31.968 --> 17:34.596
-Suspended!
-Wow, suspended!

17:39.267 --> 17:42.270
Wait, is being suspended
better than being expelled?

17:42.937 --> 17:44.647
But what about college?

17:44.731 --> 17:48.067
Even places that consider practicals only
will still check your record.

17:48.943 --> 17:50.904
No.

17:50.987 --> 17:53.782
As long as it's not for school violence,
it won't appear on her record.

17:53.865 --> 17:55.366
-Really?
-As far as I know.

17:55.450 --> 17:58.119
Whatever happens, it was my fault,
so I have to accept it.

17:59.496 --> 18:01.414
Don't be so serious.

18:01.498 --> 18:03.082
It's just a suspension!

18:07.921 --> 18:09.672
-Oh, it's Mr. Ga.
-It's Mr. Ga.

18:12.258 --> 18:15.136
CHAPTER 47:
BECAUSE YOU'RE MY FIRST STUDENT

18:15.220 --> 18:17.180
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

18:26.815 --> 18:28.441
As you've probably already heard,

18:29.067 --> 18:30.568
Eui-ju has been suspended.

18:35.448 --> 18:38.117
It's only correct that she takes
responsibility for her actions.

18:38.201 --> 18:39.494
However,

18:39.577 --> 18:41.079
it's also partly my fault.

18:42.580 --> 18:44.916
As a teacher,
I shouldn't favor any one student,

18:45.542 --> 18:46.709
and in that, I failed.

18:49.546 --> 18:51.339
If anyone was hurt by what has happened,

18:52.298 --> 18:53.508
I apologize.

18:56.010 --> 18:58.596
From now on,
I'll listen to all of you more.

18:58.680 --> 19:01.349
So instead of taking sides
about who was right or wrong,

19:01.432 --> 19:04.018
I hope you'll try
to understand each other.

19:04.602 --> 19:05.812
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

19:06.938 --> 19:08.648
Okay, enjoy class. I'll see you later.

19:09.566 --> 19:11.025
I'm sorry.

19:12.026 --> 19:12.944
Sorry.

19:16.364 --> 19:17.282
Thanks.

19:36.593 --> 19:37.427
What now?

19:38.469 --> 19:41.514
I didn't get the chance
to properly thank you.

19:42.265 --> 19:43.516
Thank you, Mr. Ga.

19:45.101 --> 19:46.311
There's no need.

19:47.687 --> 19:48.730
By the way,

19:49.564 --> 19:50.940
Mr. Ga,

19:51.024 --> 19:52.609
why did you do it?

19:53.902 --> 19:54.736
What?

19:55.695 --> 19:59.532
You convinced
the principal and the other teachers

19:59.616 --> 20:01.284
to be on my side

20:01.367 --> 20:02.660
when I'm just a silly nobody.

20:18.676 --> 20:19.719
To me, you're…

20:29.145 --> 20:30.229
Because you're…

20:38.446 --> 20:39.656
my first student.

20:47.580 --> 20:48.665
Just because

20:50.083 --> 20:51.459
I'm your student?

20:55.088 --> 20:56.798
Whether Ji-a, Ha-su, or you,

20:57.465 --> 21:00.009
you're all kids
I have to turn the other cheek to.

21:03.471 --> 21:05.807
Don't get into trouble
while you're suspended.

21:05.890 --> 21:07.141
Now, go home.

21:29.914 --> 21:34.836
CHAPTER 48:
TURN OVER A NEW LEAF

21:35.795 --> 21:37.797
What? You can't eat this.

21:37.880 --> 21:40.341
Suni, go and wake Eui-ju.

21:40.883 --> 21:42.552
All right.

21:48.683 --> 21:49.726
Bang.

22:05.158 --> 22:06.159
YEO EUI-JU

22:15.710 --> 22:16.711
I'm giving it a shot too.

22:21.924 --> 22:23.885
I've always run away
without seeing things through,

22:25.094 --> 22:26.429
but I'm done with that.

22:29.974 --> 22:31.267
What do you mean?

22:31.350 --> 22:32.685
Who are you talking about?

22:37.982 --> 22:38.941
Are you going somewhere?

22:39.692 --> 22:40.526
What's this about?

22:43.154 --> 22:45.073
MURIM GIRLS' HIGH SCHOOL

22:46.324 --> 22:47.533
What's this?

22:48.326 --> 22:51.079
I know we're supposed to get you tofu,
but this should do the trick.

22:51.662 --> 22:54.248
-Isn't this actually…
-It's for the better.

22:54.332 --> 22:55.541
Don't fuss like she served time.

22:55.625 --> 22:57.126
-What?
-It's pretty much the same.

22:57.210 --> 22:59.545
-Yeah.
-Think of her as being released.

22:59.629 --> 23:01.172
It's time to turn over a new leaf, buddy.

23:01.255 --> 23:02.256
Of course.

23:02.340 --> 23:03.633
Thanks, buddy.

23:05.218 --> 23:06.552
-Isn't it so nice?
-Here.

23:06.636 --> 23:07.887
Eat these when you write.

23:07.970 --> 23:09.972
Can't have you go hungry, right?

23:10.056 --> 23:11.432
-Wow, that's expensive.
-Thanks.

23:11.516 --> 23:13.101
-How sweet!
-It's nothing.

23:13.184 --> 23:14.560
I can't believe my friend

23:15.603 --> 23:17.772
is a mega-hit writer!

23:17.855 --> 23:19.857
Eui-ju, you got this.

23:19.941 --> 23:21.192
-You got this!
-You got this!

23:21.275 --> 23:23.194
-You got this!
-You're amazing!

23:23.277 --> 23:24.570
-Go on!
-Try it!

23:24.654 --> 23:26.197
You have to eat something white

23:26.280 --> 23:27.824
-to mark your fresh start.
-I'll be good.

23:27.907 --> 23:28.950
To a fresh start!

23:47.468 --> 23:48.302
I…

23:49.720 --> 23:52.765
didn't like that Mr. Ga
was giving you so much attention.

23:56.185 --> 23:58.479
I thought if I ruined you,

23:58.563 --> 24:00.940
he would notice me.

24:03.484 --> 24:04.819
But that's not what happened.

24:07.822 --> 24:09.282
I'm not trying to make excuses.

24:10.825 --> 24:12.535
I just wanted to tell you

24:13.828 --> 24:15.121
that I'm sorry.

24:24.297 --> 24:28.759
It's thanks to you that
I was able to acknowledge my mistakes.

24:28.843 --> 24:30.428
If none of this had happened,

24:30.511 --> 24:32.930
I would've kept writing
with a sense of guilt.

24:42.231 --> 24:43.399
Let's get to the auditorium.

24:44.066 --> 24:46.402
The auditorium? Not homeroom?

24:46.485 --> 24:49.113
There's a special lecture
by Professor Na Deul-i.

24:49.197 --> 24:52.241
Do you think she's Mr. Ga's girlfriend?

24:52.325 --> 24:54.827
One, two, this is a mic test. Check.

24:54.911 --> 24:55.870
Say ho, ho, ho!

24:55.953 --> 24:56.871
-Ho, ho, ho!
-Ho, ho, ho!

24:59.040 --> 25:02.793
Dan-ji wants me to bring
the projector remote from the AV room.

25:02.877 --> 25:03.878
You go ahead.

25:03.961 --> 25:04.879
Okay.

25:20.311 --> 25:21.479
Hello.

25:22.104 --> 25:23.147
Oh, hello.

25:24.398 --> 25:26.734
You're the student I met
at the coffee shop that time, right?

25:28.819 --> 25:30.279
It's nice to see a familiar face.

25:31.405 --> 25:33.699
I'm shaking with nerves.

25:34.575 --> 25:35.576
Why?

25:37.536 --> 25:40.289
I've never really interacted
with teenagers.

25:41.249 --> 25:42.792
I hear teenagers these days can be scary.

25:43.542 --> 25:45.127
I'm worried I might say the wrong thing.

25:47.088 --> 25:48.422
We're not that bad.

25:49.006 --> 25:50.925
We don't bite unless you try
and steal our food.

25:59.141 --> 26:00.643
Are you here for this?

26:00.726 --> 26:02.353
-Yes, sir.
-Let's go.

26:03.437 --> 26:04.647
Do you think I'll be okay?

26:05.648 --> 26:08.025
Why not? You've lectured
to a bigger audience before.

26:08.109 --> 26:10.736
I still feel nervous, all right?

26:12.863 --> 26:14.073
Wish me luck!

26:16.784 --> 26:18.286
You'll be fine.

26:18.369 --> 26:20.746
I'm telling you it's my first time
somewhere like this.

26:27.628 --> 26:28.504
Eui-ju.

26:29.505 --> 26:30.506
What did she want?

26:30.589 --> 26:31.841
We made up.

26:32.800 --> 26:33.884
Made up?

26:33.968 --> 26:34.969
Yeah, made up.

26:37.972 --> 26:41.142
IN MY OWN WAY,
AT A PACE THAT SUITS ME

26:43.227 --> 26:45.855
Hello, everyone.
It's great to be here. I'm Na Deul-i.

26:46.772 --> 26:49.317
I've put together some photos
to show you who I am.

26:49.400 --> 26:50.776
What do you think this is?

26:50.860 --> 26:53.362
It's the first test I ever took
back in first grade.

26:54.322 --> 26:56.532
Weird, right? I'm supposed to be a genius.

26:57.283 --> 26:59.452
What do you consider
when choosing a career?

26:59.535 --> 27:01.454
-Prestige.
-Prestige? Money? Yes, money.

27:01.537 --> 27:05.708
In STEM, is the MBTI T-type
really more common?

27:05.791 --> 27:07.960
"Are you a T-type?
Are you a freaking T-type?"

27:08.044 --> 27:09.712
Studies have discovered a high likelihood.

27:09.795 --> 27:12.006
You should try it for yourselves.

27:12.089 --> 27:16.761
At the time, I was certain
Team Korea would finish first.

27:16.844 --> 27:20.056
But right at the last moment,
someone ended up dropping out,

27:20.139 --> 27:22.099
so we only finished second.

27:22.183 --> 27:23.351
Who do you think that was?

27:26.062 --> 27:29.857
Yes, sitting at the back,
your math teacher, Mr. Ga.

27:34.820 --> 27:38.783
I believe someday
you'll each find your own answer.

27:39.575 --> 27:40.576
It's so annoying.

27:41.494 --> 27:42.661
Why is she so damn cool?

27:44.246 --> 27:45.206
I'll be cheering you on.

27:45.831 --> 27:48.459
This is Na Deul-i signing off.

27:48.959 --> 27:49.960
Thank you.

27:58.469 --> 27:59.804
One, two, three.

28:01.889 --> 28:03.140
I'll share it later. Go back in.

28:03.224 --> 28:04.975
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

28:05.059 --> 28:06.685
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

28:06.769 --> 28:08.020
-Please take a photo of me.
-Sir.

28:08.104 --> 28:10.064
-Me too.
-One for me too, sir!

28:12.608 --> 28:14.276
Ready. One, two, three.

28:15.736 --> 28:17.696
-Thank you.
-Can I get one too?

28:17.780 --> 28:19.281
-Nice!
-Thank you.

28:19.365 --> 28:21.242
-One at a time?
-Yes, sir.

28:21.325 --> 28:22.326
Oh, thank you.

28:24.245 --> 28:25.579
One, two, three.

28:26.956 --> 28:28.207
-Thank you.
-One, two, three.

28:29.291 --> 28:30.626
-You're so cool.
-Thank you.

28:30.709 --> 28:32.670
Thank you, Professor. Thank you, sir.

28:37.466 --> 28:38.426
Come over here.

28:40.261 --> 28:41.679
Okay. One, two, three.

28:44.432 --> 28:45.391
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

28:45.975 --> 28:48.769
Thanks to you,
I could relax and do a good job.

28:48.853 --> 28:49.854
Thank you so much.

28:51.730 --> 28:53.649
She helped me deal with my nerves.

28:56.861 --> 28:59.530
There's a pop quiz for after-school math.
Go write it on the board.

29:00.114 --> 29:01.949
-Yes, sir.
-Off you go.

29:02.616 --> 29:03.951
-Goodbye.
-Bye.

29:05.119 --> 29:06.245
Let's go.

29:07.788 --> 29:08.873
-Did you take it?
-Yes.

29:12.960 --> 29:16.130
Wow, they do look good together.

29:19.967 --> 29:21.010
Sorry.

29:25.306 --> 29:26.557
You don't need to tell me.

29:27.266 --> 29:29.268
They look picture-perfect.

29:33.522 --> 29:34.356
Let's go.

29:36.901 --> 29:39.069
You happy to research alone
instead of joining me in the US?

29:39.153 --> 29:43.532
CHAPTER 49:
THE ABSOLUT VALUE OF ROMANCE

29:43.616 --> 29:44.992
So, from now on, we'll be competing.

29:46.827 --> 29:48.037
To see who gets there first.

29:48.120 --> 29:51.123
Or rather, who gets there at all.

29:52.833 --> 29:55.461
Yeah, time will tell

29:56.212 --> 29:58.422
the value of useless pure mathematics.

30:00.424 --> 30:02.009
Don't come crying to me later.

30:05.012 --> 30:06.305
Just get in already.

30:07.056 --> 30:08.807
Okay, I'm going.

30:10.476 --> 30:12.061
-See you.
-Bye!

30:13.395 --> 30:15.856
VISITOR PARKING LOT

30:28.869 --> 30:30.955
-Good afternoon.
-Good afternoon.

30:31.038 --> 30:32.414
We're having a pop quiz today.

30:32.498 --> 30:33.958
You've got 20 minutes.

30:34.041 --> 30:34.959
Pass them back.

30:53.269 --> 30:54.728
PAST MATH EXAM QUESTIONS

31:01.193 --> 31:02.486
3. PROPERTIES OF LOGARITHMIC FUNCTIONS

31:02.570 --> 31:04.738
1. DIFFERENTIATION OF POLYNOMIAL FUNCTIONS
2. MEAN VALUE THEOREM

31:30.889 --> 31:32.224
If you're done, hand it in and go.

32:06.175 --> 32:07.217
Time's up. Bring it here.

32:11.430 --> 32:12.681
I said bring it here.

32:36.538 --> 32:37.623
Put it here and go.

33:20.207 --> 33:22.501
Something that stands on its own

33:22.584 --> 33:24.753
independent of comparison.

33:24.837 --> 33:29.508
Something without conditions,
restrictions, or rivals

33:29.591 --> 33:31.176
is called an absolut value.

33:31.969 --> 33:34.388
Find the absolut value
of the following romance.

33:38.976 --> 33:41.478
What is the absolut value of
glasses divided by pigeon

33:41.562 --> 33:43.188
multiplied by the square root
of emergency room

33:43.272 --> 33:46.608
plus the square
of after-school classes plus novel

33:46.692 --> 33:49.236
multiplied by the limit of bus stop?

34:18.891 --> 34:22.269
ABSOLUTE
ABSOLUTE

34:23.061 --> 34:24.813
-Unbelievable.
-Don't you know how to spell?

34:26.899 --> 34:28.192
Of course, I do.

34:29.318 --> 34:30.486
That's just

34:31.069 --> 34:33.113
a literary device I used because I wanted

34:33.864 --> 34:35.699
to emphasize the word "absolute."

34:38.243 --> 34:40.329
Both your spelling
and your formula are a mess.

34:41.830 --> 34:43.165
Does it even have an answer?

34:43.248 --> 34:44.208
Of course.

34:44.291 --> 34:46.043
I've been working
on this problem alone lately.

34:46.752 --> 34:47.586
So what's the solution?

34:49.838 --> 34:50.798
There is

34:52.174 --> 34:53.509
only one possible answer.

34:57.930 --> 34:59.014
To me…

35:04.978 --> 35:05.979
To me,

35:06.980 --> 35:07.981
the answer is…

35:15.864 --> 35:17.074
The absolut value…

35:21.620 --> 35:23.080
is you, Mr. Ga.

35:28.293 --> 35:30.295
I'm saying my absolut value of romance

35:32.089 --> 35:33.674
is you, Mr. Ga.

36:58.216 --> 37:00.218
Subtitle: Paul Carver
